# The script `mise run bundle-test` has the headless mode of a copy of the
# editor run inside a staged bundle, and `mise run app-check` inside a copy
# of the built Leanmacs.app, each with no directory argument, an empty
# environment and a working directory outside the bundle. The config in
# `config/` is elaborated on the modules the bundle holds. What it prints
# must be exactly `expected`.

# This settle waits up to 90 s, three times the default 30 s. It is the
# first reload of bundle-test's chain: a cold, interpreted elaboration of a
# config that imports `Lean` from about 1.3 GB of module files just copied
# into the staged bundle. It takes under a second on a desktop (0.7 to 1.3 s
# at 34b68158 and at dcbe3ebf alike) and passed well inside 30 s on CI
# before b4a4eaf4. Since then, on the macos-26 runner, it overlaps
# ffi-test's cargo build and cargo-deny steps, and it ran out at 30 s in
# runs 44751682483 and 44757431162. A reload that never ends still fails
# here, naming this line and the 90000 ms.
reload
settle 90000

# `squares` is config's: it runs interpreted, calling compiled code of
# `Init` and of `Editor`. Text 0 is the scratch buffer's.
run squares
show
